This small example checks a full window just before it ends, then exactly at its end.

```javascript
const state = { windowStart: 50, count: 3 };
function windowEnded(now) {
  return now >= state.windowStart + 1000;
}
console.log(windowEnded(1049));
console.log(windowEnded(1050));
```

The outputs are false and true. At 1050, reset the count before checking the new request.
